Hey!

10
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,320
Don't just stand around.

11
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:44,209
Hurry up and go fetch
the medical team now.

12
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,100
Move it.

13
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,700
Don't lose sight of those two.

14
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,965
Slow them down and report
their location to us.

15
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,320
Damn Yamato.

16
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,979
Are you sure you're all right, sir?

17
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:03,433
You took a pretty major beating yourself

18
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,310
Fair point.

19
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,107
He did clock me pretty good.

20
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:09,277
Oh my jaw feels a little loose.

21
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,017
That's all that hurts Where
the hell are the medics?

22
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,335
This is an emergency.

23
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:15,060
Sorry for the wait, sir

24
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:29,000
That light is super annoying!

25
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,220
Papa! Wow!

26
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,660
Pray for me!

27
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:42,220
I got a light-threatening boo-boo!

28
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,460
If you're in pain, lie back down.

29
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,311
What's with the attitude?

30
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,518
Shouldn't you be happy I'm not dead?

31
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:56,440
Ow, get that nasty, Yamato.

32
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:00,700
How dare that bastard use Commander
Kaido's thunder bagua on me?

33
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,571
Well, I guess she's fine.

34
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,700
More like blunder bad, am I right?

35
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,000
Not like it hurt anyway.

36
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,720
Come on, sis.

37
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:14,358
Sorry to interrupt.

38
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,497
Both the enemies are currently
stopped in the hall, sir.

39
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,410
Perfect.

40
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:20,610
Hey!

41
00:03:20,693 --> 00:03:21,523
Papa!

42
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,040
Aren't you forgetting someone?

43
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,980
Where are you taking me?

44
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:33,140
If you got something to
say, just tell me here.

45
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,280
Don't be hasty.

46
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,695
I promise you this will not take long.

47
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,300
Get out of my way.

48
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:55,940
Please, just hear me out!

49
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,540
Just say it already!

50
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,440
There are people listening.

51
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,366
We must go somewhere private.

52
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:26,140
I said no!

53
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,317
I warned ya!

54
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,880
Jungle Palace!

55
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,200
Stubberin, aren't you?

56
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,940
Red Park!

57
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:07,890
Impressive!

58
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:10,460
You remind me of someone I once spot.

59
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,600
Damn it all. They're gone.

60
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,240
What's going on?

61
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,242
Where's Yamato?

62
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:27,756
I'm sorry, sir, but we lost
sight of the both of them.

63
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:38,540
Surely you all remember
when Kozuki Oden died, yes?

64
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:43,560
It was the very same day that Oden
Castle went down in a sea of flame.

65
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:47,757
You know, there is a mystery
lingering from back then.

66
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:50,428
A group of people
disappeared into thin air.

67
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:54,540
This little brat sent his
Akazaya Samurai Lockheed.

68
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,900
And where did those fugitives go?

69
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,260
To the future.

70
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:08,520
To be precise, they traveled
exactly 20 years through time.

71
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:09,820
Do you get it?

72
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,257
That's why they're here
in the land of Wano

73
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:14,869
looking the same age
as they did back then.

74
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:19,080
And who was responsible
for this dangerous magic?

75
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:21,480
A treacherous witch.

76
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,760
Odin's wretched wife Kozuki Toki.

77
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:31,080
She thought she could send him here
to kill me, but now I have a son.

78
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:47,720
We all know that the Kozuki family died
out ages ago, ain't that right, brother?

79
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:54,680
Damn statement, some real funny stuff!

80
00:06:56,520 --> 00:07:01,620
Hey, hey, Shogun Order Chief, why
don't you come down here with us, bro?

81
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,957
There's no need for you
to get your hands dirty.

82
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:08,040
Let me at him and I'll
gouge his friggin' eyes out.

83
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:10,660
How dare you call my mother a witch?

84
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,412
I shall personally make you pay for that.

85
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:17,900
You dare to challenge me,
you insolent little louse?

86
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,240
I wonder how I should kill you.

87
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,420
A stabbing? A shooting?

88
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:25,980
Or perhaps I should boil you alive?

89
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,740
Do you have any suggestions, boss?

90
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,532
We have to do something.

91
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:31,570
They'll kill him.

92
00:07:31,653 --> 00:07:34,091
We must maintain our trust in the Samurai.

93
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:37,100
It's a delicate situation. Be patient.

94
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:41,440
Lord Momonosuke, stay strong.

95
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,140
How awful.

96
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,220
We are so close.

97
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:53,060
The samurai gaze on helplessly as momonosuke
suffers, but maintain their secrecy,

98
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:55,991
blending in seamlessly at the celebration.

99
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:02,377
Meanwhile raw submarine
the polar tang reaches its

100
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:06,077
destination delivering his crew
and several Samurai to the rear

101
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:11,777
of Onigashima adjust trim

102
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:14,577
by 38 degrees i'm on it brace

103
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:19,220
yourselves Get us as close to
the island as you can yes sir

104
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:28,574
This is a tricky spot We don't want
to get mixed up in all those currents

105
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:45,760
It's just as bad as above Once we surface
we'll only have one shot I understand

106
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:53,000
We're counting on you traffy Get us there
Beppo, Chouchou, Penguin, is everyone ready?

107
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,417
Aye aye, Captain!

108
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,580
Aye aye, sir!

109
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,120
Take us to Kaido!

110
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,320
Away we go!

111
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,540
Call systems clear!

112
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,939
We're ready to surface at any time!

113
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:09,200
Okay, on my call, now!

114
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:33,340
There's snowing.

115
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,540
Go!

116
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,320
...and shambles.

117
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,500
They're gone now.

118
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,000
Let's pull the doors closed.

119
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,440
Time to resubmerge. Roger!

120
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,252
Ready for rapid descent!

121
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:16,340
Well, friends, we've made it.

122
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:19,567
Your ability is quite
extraordinary, Sir Law.

123
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,912
There are two entrances.

124
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,480
I can expect to see Kaido up top.

125
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:28,870
Hey!

126
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,824
Why do you gotta always
have to be so mean, huh?

127
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:35,548
I'm just saying you got us into
this mess in the first place.

128
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:37,780
Hey, wait!

129
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,760
I know that, Yelp!

130
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:57,470
Ah!

131
00:10:57,553 --> 00:10:59,332
Yagara could've warned me about the drop.

132
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,080
Oh, it's Cat Viper!

133
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:02,400
Look at you.

134
00:11:02,580 --> 00:11:04,620
You've gotten so much bigger. Huh?

135
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:07,400
You're alive! Kawamatsu!

136
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:08,770
Huh?

137
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:10,170
Ashura!

138
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,788
Is that really you, Yagara?

139
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Indeed it is. Been a while.

140
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:16,280
Here we go.

141
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:17,810
Marco!

142
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:22,160
Did you, Karoo, carry him
here? Mm-hmm. And I'm beat.

143
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,712
Carrying two people ain't easy, you know.

144
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,860
There's two? What?

145
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:28,530
Wait.

146
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:38,770
Iso!

147
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,140
It's really you?

148
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,020
My brother!

149
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:17,520
Kiku, what a fine samurai you've become.

150
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:18,950
Izo!

151
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,800
I just did not to eat us!

152
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:24,472
I thought you might never return to Wano.

153
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:25,890
Right.

154
00:12:25,973 --> 00:12:27,799
Sorry I didn't mention Izo earlier.

155
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:31,717
Marco said he knew where to find
him, so I went to go pick him up.

156
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,271
Figured we could use him.

157
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:34,490
Greetings.

158
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,417
You guys haven't changed one bit.

159
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,560
You're too kind.

160
00:12:37,860 --> 00:12:41,095
We'll have time to catch up
on the good old days later.

161
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,917
There is a strange shadow that
I spotted on the way here.

162
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,824
I'd like to go and check it out

163
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:52,220
It's great to see you Karoo! Be safe.

164
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,560
I'm glad I survived long
enough to see this day!

165
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,260
Kaido's reign will end tonight?

166
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:09,057
Where the hell is Lin-Lin?

167
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:10,457
Is she ready to go yet?

168
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,760
Actually, she is!

169
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,765
Big Mom is dressed and
already on her way, sir!

170
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:18,778
You should have told me that
as soon as you got here.

171
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,100
Uh, whoopsies.

172
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,230
Let's hurry.

173
00:13:25,313 --> 00:13:29,808
Momonosuke's execution will be the perfect
place for my official announcement.

174
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,180
Time to go.

175
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:41,250
No!

176
00:13:41,333 --> 00:13:45,100
Let's raise a toast to the
death of the Kojo-Keyo!

177
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,440
Commander Call!

178
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,540
The man in the hour is here!

179
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:06,740
Time to party!

180
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,900
All right.

181
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,960
Listen up everyone,

182
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:25,600
this execution is depressing as
hell, so I'm gonna liven things up.

183
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:33,640
It's time for the new Onigashima Project!

184
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,100
You got five minutes?

185
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:02,420
I thank you.

186
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:08,760
When I was young, I told my father
I want to become Kozuki Oden.

187
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,890
Huh?

188
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:13,057
He clobbered me good after that.

189
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:15,857
I don't see why I gotta hear
your life story right now?

190
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:18,100
Come on! Get to the point!

191
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:21,600
I was there 20 years
ago at Odin's execution.

192
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:26,240
I saw the hour of
legends with my own eyes.

193
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:29,149
The world will never
see a greater samurai.

194
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:33,420
And my father and Odichi
are the ones who slayed him.

195
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,860
I can never forgive him.

196
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:39,080
I was disgusted, of course.

197
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,600
But I was moved as well.

198
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:45,180
As I cried, I felt a rumbling in my soul.

199
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:51,600
And then one day, I happened upon
something while I was in Kuri.

200
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:56,600
It was Kozuki Odin's logbook.

201
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,360
His journal?

202
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,350
Yes.

203
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:05,220
I live by these passages.

204
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:08,880
My father and his crew
don't know this item exists.

205
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,797
Odin's grand adventures
and everything important

206
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:14,817
to him are inscribed
upon these very pages.

207
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:20,700
Now that the Akazaya Samurai are dead,
someone must carry on Odin's will.

208
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:23,000
That's why.

209
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:27,620
I will open this country to the world!

210
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,620
Wait a sec.

211
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,180
Please, allow me to fight alongside you.

212
00:17:03,420 --> 00:17:06,832
Pretty sure you told me you
were Kaido's son a second ago.

213
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:11,060
Kozuki Oren was a man, wasn't he?

214
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,420
So I chose to become a man too.

215
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,500
I can tell you're strong.

216
00:17:17,360 --> 00:17:21,595
Even when you fought me, it was clear
you were holding back quite a bit.

217
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:30,060
You really remind me of Ace.

218
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:13,340
I knew you would show
up sooner or later. Huh?

219
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,624
Although I was a bit concerned,

220
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,997
since we failed to find any
indication that you'd snuck in.

221
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:22,492
Fortunately for us, it seems
you just got lost on the way.

222
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:27,720
But even if you're foolish, I know
quite well how persistent you are.

223
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:29,860
Nya-ha-ha! They're here!

224
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,017
You really called it!

225
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:35,924
They've been hiding away like scared little
rats ever since the boiling went down.

226
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,620
Conjito, you traitor!

227
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,660
The raid will not be happening today.

228
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,500
Oh, wait.

229
00:18:44,780 --> 00:18:45,880
Is that Izo?

230
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:48,540
You're back just in time to die.

231
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:54,055
You made some of our warriors
with their heads removed.

232
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:55,660
How very artful.

233
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:58,587
I even tried to make
them look just like you.

234
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:01,777
It's surprising you've lasted
this long without Odin.

235
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:04,117
You're powerless without him to lead you.

236
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:06,397
How quickly you forget
we still have a leader.

237
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:09,600
Lord Momonosuke will show
us the path to the future!

238
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,197
Where did you take him?

239
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,574
He had better be safe!

240
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:16,320
Even I cannot say for sure.

241
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:17,960
He's with Orochi now.

242
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:21,680
The boy did try to
escape as best he could.

243
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:27,060
These accursed tunnels
will be the death of me!

244
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,800
Get back here!

245
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:49,980
I refuse to be averted anymore!

246
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:52,260
This all ends here!

247
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:13,700
That was bold.

248
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:29,780
I can't have you getting away.

249
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:34,260
If you do, I'll be unable
to fulfill my role.

250
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:42,320
I had intended to knock
him unconscious cleanly,

251
00:20:42,540 --> 00:20:45,893
but I'm afraid that I must
have overdone it a little bit.

252
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,717
Thankfully, he has some fighting
spirit and was able to cling to life.

253
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:52,741
Imagine if I'd given the
Shogun his lifeless body.

254
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,140
Lord Momonosuke.

255
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,900
As we speak,

256
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:03,620
the Shogun is graciously ensuring that
Momonosuke's execution will be a big hit. Ha!

257
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:04,650
Ha! Ha!

258
00:21:04,733 --> 00:21:08,460
All I have to do is buy them a
little time and it all ends here.

259
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:12,741
The tale of the Kozuki clan will
officially be nothing but history.

260
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,920
Out of the way, you bastard!

261
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,160
To glory!

262
